 Start mode
⍝ Register every plugin and start the gallery. mode goes straight to EWC.Init:
⍝ 'Browser' for a single user, 'Multi' for a clone per connection, 'Desktop'
⍝ for a native window.
⍝     ]link.create ~/dev/ewc/EWC
⍝     ]link.create FireworksPlugin  ~/dev/ewc-plugins/fireworks/APLSource
⍝     ]link.create FireworksApp     ~/dev/ewc-plugins/fireworks/app
⍝     ]link.create GlobePlugin      ~/dev/ewc-plugins/globe/APLSource
⍝     ]link.create GlobeApp         ~/dev/ewc-plugins/globe/app
⍝     ]link.create ApexChartsPlugin ~/dev/ewc-plugins/apexcharts/APLSource
⍝     ]link.create ApexApp          ~/dev/ewc-plugins/apexcharts/app
⍝     ]link.create KendoPlugin      ~/dev/ewc-plugins/kendo/APLSource
⍝     ]link.create KendoApp         ~/dev/ewc-plugins/kendo/app
⍝     ]link.create Gallery          ~/dev/ewc-plugins/gallery/app
⍝     Gallery.Start 'Browser'
⍝ Beware hard-coded port, but this is a demo only
 EWC←#.EWC
 EWC.PORT←22322

 #.FireworksPlugin.Register
 #.GlobePlugin.Register
 #.ApexChartsPlugin.Register
 #.KendoPlugin.Register
 EWC.Init mode

 ⎕←'Open http://localhost:',(⍕EWC.PORT),'/'
